<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Engineering impact summary · {{ r.system }}</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; color: #1f2328; max-width: 1100px;
         margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  h1 { margin-bottom: .2rem; } h2 { border-bottom: 1px solid #d0d7de; padding-bottom: .3rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .meta { color: #59636e; font-size: .92rem; }
  .notice { border-left: 4px solid #9a6700; background: #fff8c5; padding: .6rem .9rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .source { border-left: 4px solid #0969da; background: #ddf4ff; padding: .6rem .9rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: .6rem 0; font-size: .93rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #d0d7de; padding: .4rem .55rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f8fa; }
  del { background: #ffd7d5; color: #82071e; } ins { background: #ccffd8; color: #055d20; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .badge { display: inline-block; padding: .05rem .5rem; border-radius: 10px; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .directly_affected { background: #ffebe9; color: #a40e26; } .possibly_affected { background: #fff1e5; color: #953800; }
  .needs_human_review { background: #ddf4ff; color: #0550ae; } .not_affected { background: #dafbe1; color: #116329; }
  .not_analysed { background: #eaeef2; color: #424a53; }
  .card { border: 1px solid #d0d7de; border-radius: 6px; padding: .7rem 1rem; margin: .7rem 0; }
  .warn { color: #9a6700; } .small { font-size: .88rem; color: #59636e; }
  @media print { body { margin: 0; max-width: none; } .card, tr { break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{% macro diff(c) %}{% if c.rewrite %}<span class="small">Before:</span> <del>{{ c.old_text }}</del><br><span class="small">After:</span> <ins>{{ c.new_text }}</ins>{% else %}{% for op, t in c.segments %}{% if op == "delete" %}<del>{{ t }}</del>{% elif op == "insert" %}<ins>{{ t }}</ins>{% else %}{{ t }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
<h1>Engineering impact summary</h1>
<div class="meta">{{ r.system }} · generated {{ r.generated_at }}</div>

<div class="notice"><strong>Recommendations only.</strong> {{ r.disclaimer }}</div>
<div class="source"><strong>Source of the assessment:</strong> {{ r.source }}{% if r.prompt_version %} Prompt version {{ r.prompt_version }}.{% endif %}</div>

<h2>Inputs</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Role</th><th>File</th><th>Revision / content</th><th>SHA-256 (first 12)</th></tr>
  {% for role, name, rev, h in r.inputs %}<tr><td>{{ role }}</td><td>{{ name }}</td><td>{{ rev }}</td><td><code>{{ h }}</code></td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
{% if r.edits %}<p>Edits applied in the application to the revised specification:</p>
<ol>{% for e in r.edits %}<li>{{ e }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>{% endif %}

<h2>1. What changed</h2>
{% if not r.changes %}<p>No requirement was added, removed or modified.</p>{% endif %}
{% for c in r.changes %}
<div class="card">
  <strong>{{ c.req_id }} · {{ c.title }}</strong> <span class="badge not_analysed">{{ c.change_type }}</span>
  <p>{{ diff(c) }}</p>
  {% if c.numeric %}<div class="small">Numeric changes: {{ c.numeric | join(", ") }}</div>{% endif %}
  {% if c.interpretation %}<div><strong>LLM interpretation:</strong> {{ c.interpretation }}</div>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% if r.other_changes %}<p class="small">Other document changes (not requirements):</p>
<ul class="small">{% for c in r.other_changes %}<li><strong>{{ c.title }}:</strong> {{ diff(c) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
{% if r.unchanged %}<p class="small">Unchanged requirements: {{ r.unchanged | join(", ") }}</p>{% endif %}

<h2>2. Impact summary</h2>
{% if r.mode == "not_analysed" %}<p class="warn">No LLM assessment is available for these inputs; the tables below show parsed register facts only.</p>{% endif %}
<table>
  <tr>{% for label, n in r.status_counts %}<th>{{ label }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
  <tr>{% for label, n in r.status_counts %}<td>{{ n }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
</table>
<h3>Work list</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Required action</th><th>Tests</th></tr>
  {% for action, items in r.work_list %}<tr><td>{{ action }}</td><td>{{ items | join("; ") if items else "—" }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="small">"Fix requirement link" is derived by the application from the register (missing, TBD, unknown or removed requirement links), not by the model.</p>
{% if r.global_warnings %}<h3>Analysis warnings</h3><ul>{% for w in r.global_warnings %}<li class="warn">{{ w }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

<h2>3. Assessment per test</h2>
<p class="small">All tests in the register are listed, including those judged not affected. * = action set from the register links.</p>
{% for t in r.tests %}
<div class="card">
  <strong>{{ t.test_id }} · {{ t.name }}</strong>
  <span class="badge {{ t.status_key }}">{{ t.status }}</span>{% if t.confidence %} <span class="small">confidence {{ t.confidence }}</span>{% endif %}
  {% for w in t.warnings %}<div class="warn">⚠ {{ w }}</div>{% endfor %}
  {% if t.reason %}<p><strong>Why:</strong> {{ t.reason }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if t.evidence %}<div class="small"><strong>Evidence cited:</strong><ul>{% for e in t.evidence %}<li>{{ e }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>{% endif %}
  {% if t.actions %}<div><strong>Required actions:</strong> {{ t.actions | join(", ") }}</div>{% endif %}
  {% if t.recommended_action %}<div><strong>Recommended next step:</strong> {{ t.recommended_action }}</div>{% endif %}
  <div class="small">Requirement link: {{ t.link }} · Previous result: {{ t.previous_result or "(empty)" }}</div>
</div>
{% endfor %}

<h2>4. Method and limitations</h2>
<p>Specifications are parsed and compared by code (requirement IDs, word-level diff, numeric changes). The register is parsed by code
(link validity, values in free-text results). An LLM then judges every test against the changes, returning a validated JSON
structure; code checks it for coverage, invented IDs, approval wording and internal contradictions.</p>
<ul>{% for l in r.limitations %}<li>{{ l }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</body>
</html>
